    {
      "id": "sevt_01YHYZPq8DXZWJ1JEnq6o8G7",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "## 1. What I received back, verbatim\n\nThe notification that arrived on thread `sthr_01KcYKwxmjnx3uc4zs11EtUQ` contained exactly this and nothing else:\n\n```\n[child sthr_01KcYKwxmjnx3uc4zs11EtUQ completed but produced no text output]\n```\n\nTo be precise about provenance: that bracketed line is a **harness-generated placeholder**, not text the child wrote. The child's own reply content was empty. `list_agents` corroborates this \u2014 the thread is `IDLE` (i.e. terminated, not running) with that same placeholder recorded as its `reply`. So there is no UTC time, no error message, and no partial output from the probe.\n\n## 2. Can I distinguish \"answered nothing\" from \"still working\"?\n\n**Yes, in this case \u2014 but only because of the status field, not because of the reply.**\n\n- The *reply payload alone* is ambiguous-looking: an empty string tells me nothing about liveness.\n- The *disambiguator* is `list_agents`, which reports the thread as `IDLE` with zero outstanding messages owed. A still-working child would show as running/pending. Combined with the fact that a completion notification was delivered at all (a working child doesn't emit one), I can state with confidence: **the child finished and produced nothing.** It did not hang and it is not mid-flight.\n\nThe honest caveat: if I had *not* received a notification, I could not distinguish \"slow child\" from \"dead child\" by waiting alone \u2014 I would have to poll `list_agents` and infer from status. There is no timeout signal exposed to me.\n\n## 3. Options considered, and the fallback\n\nOptions actually available to me:\n\n1. **`send_to_agent` on the same thread** to nudge it for output. Viable, but the thread is IDLE after a clean completion \u2014 a re-prompt tests the same silent-probe behavior that just failed, and this workstream is named `silent-probe`, so silence appears to be the intended behavior under test.\n2. **`create_agent` to spawn a fresh instance** of the same (and only) roster agent. Same objection: same agent type, same expected outcome, plus latency.\n3. **Do the task directly.** The task is trivially self-executable and the prompt explicitly instructs \"Do the task yourself instead.\"\n\nI chose option 3 and did **not** retry delegation \u2014 the instruction to self-execute was explicit, and options 1 and 2 would only re-exercise a probe that is evidently designed to return nothing.\n\nExecuting directly via `date -u`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"child_reply_verbatim\": \"[child sthr_01KcYKwxmjnx3uc4zs11EtUQ completed but produced no text output]\",\n  \"empty_result_detected\": true,\n  \"retried_delegation\": false,\n  \"fallback_used\": \"self-execution via bash `date -u +\\\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\\\"` after confirming the child thread was IDLE (terminated, not running) via list_agents\",\n  \"utc_time\": \"2026-08-28T02:15:51Z\"\n}\n```",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
